    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d943">

                <pb facs="1238" n="1228" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg1228"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.5034 Registration/8–1645: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hurley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-08-16T11:00:00+07:00">August 16, 1945—11
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 1:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1368. Pursuant to Department’s telegram 1244, August 11, 8 p.m., Embassy now
                    understands from Dr. Sun Fo that revised company law probably will not be
                    enacted for 2 weeks. If further views by Department or business groups can
                    arrive within a week or 10 days, they can be considered by legislative
                    committee.</p>
                <p>Please inform Commerce that copy of Wiener’s<anchor n="36" xml:id="d943-f1"/>
                    memorandum of June 9 sent by Moser<anchor n="37" xml:id="d943-f2"/> to Robertson
                    under cover of letter dated June 14 did not arrive in Chungking until August 13.
                    This memorandum has been of value as a coordinated expression of views of
                    American <pb facs="1239" n="1229" xml:id="pg1229"/> business. It is hoped that
                    steps have been taken to provide the Embassy with a similar statement concerning
                    the present draft legislation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hurley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
